Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.52,0:00:04.48,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,{\fad(481,435)}December 24th, Stellar Year 2149
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.42,0:00:07.70,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Welcome back!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.70,0:00:09.44,Main,Theresa,0,0,0,,Welcome home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.90,0:00:13.88,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I'm so happy you're back safe!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.88,0:00:16.64,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,It's important to get off the \Nfront lines so you can rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.64,0:00:19.00,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I got you all gifts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.49,0:00:22.01,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Man, the year just flew by!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.01,0:00:24.46,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,This is your second Holy Birth Festival!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.46,0:00:27.75,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I'm happy that this time, \NI got to give you your presents!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.66,0:00:31.63,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,I'm home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.84,0:00:32.86,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,I'm home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.20,0:00:34.35,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,I'm home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.58,0:00:35.64,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,I'm home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.51,0:00:37.48,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I'm home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.54,0:00:41.72,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'm happy for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.18,0:00:44.04,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.33,0:00:45.98,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Time for a party!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.98,0:00:48.61,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Are your arithmetic drills done?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.99,0:00:52.83,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Your punishments always teach me so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.22,0:02:15.86,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Independent Mobile Force...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.86,0:02:20.85,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Basically it means we kick Legion ass, \Nlike we've always done.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.85,0:02:25.62,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Yes, this is a proposal from me, \Nas an individual,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.62,0:02:28.25,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,to grant your request \Nto fight on the front lines.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.64,0:02:33.00,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,The issue is the foreign officer \Nwho will serve as your commander...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.98,0:02:37.53,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,I'm okay with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.53,0:02:38.59,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Fine by me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.59,0:02:39.44,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.44,0:02:40.06,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Yup.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.86,0:02:42.36,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Shin, what do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.08,0:02:53.45,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,Western Theater forces \Nsustained 60% losses.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.45,0:02:55.63,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,We're speeding up the curriculum \Nat all our officer training schools,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.63,0:02:59.89,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,specialist training schools, and boot camps \Nto replace the lost manpower.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.89,0:03:02.69,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,But they won't have the training they need.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.69,0:03:06.25,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,And while the Legion \Nlost their combat forces,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.25,0:03:08.77,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,their manufacturing facilities are unharmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.19,0:03:13.45,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,The war situation's only going to get worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.90,0:03:15.50,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,So unless something changes,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.50,0:03:20.18,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,humanity will be slowly worn down \Nuntil we finally lose, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.18,0:03:21.00,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.00,0:03:23.74,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,We'll maintain our defense lines, \Nas we have been doing,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.74,0:03:26.55,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,while putting together \Nan independent mobile unit
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.55,0:03:29.62,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,that can bring concentrated firepower \Ndown on critical Legion areas.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.96,0:03:33.06,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,I didn't expect you to put together \Nthe same plan we had.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.06,0:03:37.32,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,A mobile strike force comprised \Nentirely of Eighty-Six...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.32,0:03:40.58,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,If you'll forgive my saying so, \Nthis doesn't sound like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.92,0:03:44.21,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Sure, but they're the ones who wanted it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.78,0:03:49.46,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,They have their own values.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.46,0:03:52.72,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I don't have the right to refuse them \Nout of misplaced pity.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.04,0:03:55.80,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,If they still choose the battlefield \Nafter all that's happened,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.80,0:03:58.18,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I'd like them to be able to stay together.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.58,0:04:04.59,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,Will the Eighty-Six accept \Nthis foreign officer, though?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.59,0:04:05.94,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I talked to them already.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.52,0:04:11.63,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I was worried as well, \Nbut I guess I shouldn't have been.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.63,0:04:12.35,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,After all...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.82,0:04:21.88,Main,Woman,0,0,0,,This is from me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.74,0:04:24.82,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.36,0:04:35.14,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,It's been a long time, Eugene.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.12,0:04:39.62,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Sorry I couldn't come sooner.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.19,0:04:47.03,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Eugene, the Western Front is just\N as it was when you were there.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.35,0:04:48.94,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,It's still hanging in there, somehow.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.30,0:04:54.37,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,You asked me before why I fought, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.90,0:04:57.23,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,To be honest, I still don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.00,0:05:02.84,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I don't have a reason \Nto fight the way you did.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.02,0:05:06.31,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,But there's one thing I know, \Nand that's that I...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.70,0:05:09.60,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I promised to take them \Nall the way to the end,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.99,0:05:13.10,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,and a battlefield isn't what I want them \Nto see when they get there.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.80,0:05:22.73,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,The sea...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.56,0:05:26.67,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,The thing you wanted \Nyour sister to see someday.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.19,0:05:29.04,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I don't care about seeing it myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.32,0:05:32.94,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,But I want them to see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.63,0:05:37.39,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I think if I can show them something new, \Nsomething they've never seen before...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.09,0:05:43.13,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,That will be enough of a\N reason to fight for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.89,0:05:46.88,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I'll come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.34,0:05:50.97,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,And when I do, I'll tell you about \Nsomething you've never seen before.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.19,0:05:56.24,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Marcel.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.90,0:05:59.45,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,Nina puts them there.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.03,0:06:01.64,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,Eugene's little sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.23,0:06:07.17,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,She keeps writing letters \Nto her dead brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.96,0:06:09.27,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,It's my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.20,0:06:14.29,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.31,0:06:18.39,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,Why do you just accept it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.30,0:06:20.77,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,It was me!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.77,0:06:23.47,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,These letters... I was the one!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.83,0:06:26.72,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,I was the one who made her \Nwrite these letters to you!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.72,0:06:28.85,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,I was just so angry and frustrated,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.28,0:06:31.87,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,but I didn't want to blame myself!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.22,0:06:39.20,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,So I pretended it was all your fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.77,0:06:43.97,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.60,0:06:47.88,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.14,0:06:53.16,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.70,0:07:00.32,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I need to apologize to you. \NAnd to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.79,0:07:04.76,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.01,0:07:24.20,Main,Marcel,0,0,0,,It's good to see him smiling, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.88,0:07:40.62,Main,Nina,0,0,0,,Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.30,0:07:46.73,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Shin, you're not gonna change \Nyour personal mark?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.20,0:07:51.20,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,You don't like it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.20,0:07:53.80,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,I don't mind painting it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.80,0:07:55.73,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,But it's a bit of a bad omen...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.46,0:07:57.99,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,This is a weird thing to say,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.59,0:08:01.00,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,but do you really need \Nto carry it anymore?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.23,0:08:10.17,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Maybe you're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.17,0:08:14.08,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,But it can't be a bad omen \Nafter I've had it for six years.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.08,0:08:15.81,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,And I don't think of it as a heavy burden.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.34,0:08:17.90,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Sure, sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.21,0:08:21.99,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Looks like you're over some stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.65,0:08:25.57,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,That's how it seems to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.67,0:08:27.79,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I couldn't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.24,0:08:29.13,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.04,0:08:33.01,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I think I can see them off now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.16,0:08:41.12,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,{\fad(647,600)}March 20th, Stellar Year 2150
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.77,0:08:52.76,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.55,0:08:58.27,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,It's hard to envision a future \Nwithout my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.58,0:09:03.09,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,I don't have anything I wish for. \NAnything I'm seeking.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.91,0:09:07.60,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,I still don't know \Nwhat I'm living for.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.20,0:09:09.01,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.84,0:09:11.39,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,I'm really going to paint it, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.18,0:09:18.42,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.64,0:09:25.63,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,I have people who don't plan \Non leaving me behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.53,0:09:30.02,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,Who said I'm the one \Nthey want by their side.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.68,0:09:33.87,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,So... I think I'm okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.62,0:09:37.00,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,I think I can get there alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.66,0:09:39.72,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.12,0:09:54.13,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I know. \NI haven't forgotten you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.34,0:09:56.36,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.26,0:10:00.53,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I'm the Reaper.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.88,0:10:06.06,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,I'll fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.82,0:10:11.16,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,Because with the Legion keeping this world \Nclosed off, I can't make it happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.45,0:10:16.00,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,For their sake.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.02,0:10:18.48,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,For their sake.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.42,0:10:25.85,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,And for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.02,0:10:30.02,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,December 26th, Stellar Year 2149
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.32,0:10:49.55,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,It's thanks to you \Nthat I was able to come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.75,0:10:59.06,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I won't forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.36,0:11:32.20,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I've returned, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.43,0:11:40.67,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,A Legion offensive began on the night \Nof the Revolution Festival.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.29,0:11:44.96,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Many of my comrades fought, as did I.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.84,0:11:50.93,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Many people of the 86th district \Nanswered my call and fought with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.01,0:11:54.28,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I won't forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.46,0:12:03.60,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,But the Republic is gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.35,0:12:06.41,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,It took only a week.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.66,0:12:14.05,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,We still managed \Nto keep a defense line going,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.52,0:12:18.99,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,and after two months passed, rescue came.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.80,0:12:24.92,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,From far to the east, past Legion-held\N territory and our own borders.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.54,0:12:28.69,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,They—the Giad Federacy—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.09,0:12:34.71,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,already knew about the oppression \Nand slaughter of the Eighty-Six.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.40,0:12:39.70,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,The survivors of the 86th district were saved,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.22,0:12:44.52,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,and any one of them who wants to \Ncan become a Federacy citizen.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.32,0:12:48.00,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,The awful things have all stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.42,0:12:55.75,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,The rescue forces remain here, \Nproviding us a modicum of support, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.44,0:13:00.34,Main,Sanders,0,0,0,,Hey, he got more than I did!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.34,0:13:01.63,Main,Tom,0,0,0,,Do your jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.63,0:13:05.18,Main,John,0,0,0,,Can't you coloreds treat us equally?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.47,0:13:12.63,Main,Sanders,0,0,0,,How did it end up like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.73,0:13:21.30,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,"There can be no punishment for a citizenry \Nthat's not aware of its crimes."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.21,0:13:26.15,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,Is Uncle right, Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.82,0:13:35.50,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,Colonel Milizé?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.95,0:13:37.25,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,Is that...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.25,0:13:38.83,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Ignore it, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.51,0:13:40.97,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.12,0:13:48.69,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,As you know, it was the brave soldiers \Nof the Federacy, equipped with the latest weaponry,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.69,0:13:56.05,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,who valiantly pushed back the battle lines \Nand retook the 1st District,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.05,0:13:59.67,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,where we find ourselves today. Correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.67,0:14:00.27,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.27,0:14:04.73,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,The Federacy has requested \Nthat we send an officer to help them
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.73,0:14:09.36,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,break the stalemate north of District 1 \Nand retake the land stolen by the Legion.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.98,0:14:14.14,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,I'm told you've volunteered \Nto lead the unit assigned to this task.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.14,0:14:15.56,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,Is that correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.94,0:14:17.21,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,It is correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.63,0:14:22.68,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,As your superior officer, \NI knew you'd agree!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.68,0:14:24.51,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,I feel the same!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.51,0:14:26.65,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,Good luck out there!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.45,0:14:31.13,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,So you're going to the Federacy, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.68,0:14:32.75,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Yup.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.21,0:14:37.82,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,You're not surprised?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.82,0:14:39.30,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,After all that's happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.30,0:14:43.41,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,If something like that could surprise me, \NI would've ditched you long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.47,0:14:47.87,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,Ever since that day, \Nyou've just been full of surprises.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.37,0:15:00.12,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,I've had a lifetime's worth \Nof surprises already.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.10,0:15:07.36,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,Why? Is that possible?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.41,0:15:06.66,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.36,0:15:10.78,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,This RAID device the Federacy made!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.78,0:15:13.26,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,For some reason, \Nit has the same design as the Republic.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.03,0:15:15.79,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,Is it chance?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.79,0:15:18.01,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,No, no way in hell it's chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.77,0:15:18.01,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.01,0:15:21.25,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,The Federation made it, \Nbut it's got our tech in it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.60,0:15:25.49,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,You couldn't do this without help \Nfrom a living Eighty-Six.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.21,0:15:32.42,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,But I can't imagine any Eighty-Six making contact \Nwith the Federacy before the Legion offensive...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.23,0:15:41.16,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,Seriously...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.16,0:15:42.31,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.31,0:15:45.80,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,Well, I guess the answers\N will be waiting for us there.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.57,0:15:51.19,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Annette, why do you have \Na Federacy RAID device?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.19,0:15:52.79,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,'Cause I volunteered.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.64,0:15:56.25,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,I'm being sent as a technology officer.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.96,0:15:59.20,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,I'm going to the Federacy, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.65,0:16:06.44,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,When you said you were going \Nto do everything you could until the end,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.44,0:16:10.33,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,I stopped feeling as though \Nnothing I did would matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.89,0:16:12.69,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,It's not just me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.99,0:16:15.21,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,The others too, I think.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.32,0:16:20.98,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,So, if you're using a Para-RAID, \NI'll have to go with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.60,0:16:25.36,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,We're together again, Lena!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.12,0:16:31.10,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.34,0:16:34.30,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Oh jeez, Annette!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.24,0:16:41.72,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. \NWe're still putting things together.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.14,0:16:46.02,sign_24052_205_Unit_Roster,Onscreen,0,0,0,,Unit Roster
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.74,0:16:46.02,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,But this...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.02,0:16:49.60,Main Top,Willem,0,0,0,,It's not that we don't respect \Nyour talents, Colonel Milizé.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.19,0:16:51.11,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,{\fad(690,643)}March 12th, Stellar Year 2150
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.60,0:16:53.21,Main Top,Willem,0,0,0,,You and the Eighty-Six survived \Nthe Legion offensive.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.21,0:16:56.31,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,We're glad to have an officer like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.97,0:16:58.70,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.70,0:17:01.16,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I'll do my best until the very end.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.84,0:17:05.24,Main,Willem,0,0,0,,I'll see you in the Federacy, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.09,0:17:24.39,Flashback,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,I can buy you time, if nothing else.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.98,0:17:28.13,Flashback,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,It's time for you to be crushed, Lena,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.11,0:17:34.58,Flashback,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,as you watch your naïve dreams\N shatter against reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.92,0:17:44.00,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Uncle, give me just a bit more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.66,0:17:53.08,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Until my dream shatters.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.54,0:17:58.10,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Welcome, welcome!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.10,0:18:00.80,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,We've been waiting for you, \NBloody Regina.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.29,0:18:03.29,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Now, let's not waste any time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.54,0:18:09.89,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,There's a place I want to show you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.08,0:18:28.04,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,{\fad(690,684)}March 20th, Stellar Year 2150
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.86,0:18:38.22,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I won't forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.97,0:18:41.41,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I won't forget!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.74,0:18:44.06,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I won't forget...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.64,0:18:48.07,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I won't forget...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.42,0:18:51.98,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I won't forget...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.60,0:19:04.27,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,I'll fight... until I reach \Nthe place they reached...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.27,0:19:08.71,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,The place that can be found only by those \Nwho kept going to the very end.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.18,0:19:11.96,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,To keep fighting...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.96,0:19:19.59,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,To live life to the fullest.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.68,0:19:26.19,Italics,Lev,0,0,0,,Keep them safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.00,0:19:45.60,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,I saw her too, actually, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.01,0:19:47.73,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,I don't remember it well, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.84,0:19:51.99,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,I can't imagine the look on his face.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.11,0:19:57.49,Italics,Anju,0,0,0,,They say there's a black cat with her.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.26,0:20:03.89,Italics,Anju,0,0,0,,If only it were Kitty, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.80,0:20:08.62,Italics,Anju,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.57,0:20:10.34,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,This?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.60,0:20:13.46,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,What about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.91,0:20:18.94,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is her!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.44,0:20:23.31,Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,Theo, cut it out!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.31,0:20:25.10,Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,That won't happen with Shin!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.10,0:20:26.72,Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,The two of them aren't like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.72,0:20:29.16,Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,And I've known him longer!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.16,0:20:30.95,Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,So she's even more \Nof a little sister than me!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.86,0:20:32.93,Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,Victory's mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.88,0:20:32.93,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,{\i1}Theo!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.57,0:20:38.03,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,The perfect boy-meets-girl!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.42,0:20:39.33,Italics,Willem,0,0,0,,Beep beep.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.24,0:20:41.36,Italics,Willem,0,0,0,,Beep beep.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.82,0:20:42.77,Italics,Willem,0,0,0,,Beep!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.27,0:20:46.25,Italics,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'll surprise him, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.28,0:20:49.89,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,What was it? "Bloody Regina"?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.89,0:20:51.37,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,Yuck.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.37,0:20:52.96,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,Is that how it looks to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.37,0:20:54.02,Italics Top,Kurena,0,0,0,,Will she recognize us?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.02,0:20:56.39,Italics Top,Anju,0,0,0,,I hope she does.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.39,0:20:58.53,Italics Top,Anju,0,0,0,,But if she doesn't, \Nthat might be fun, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.66,0:21:05.76,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,I'm sorry I'm late, Mr. President.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.76,0:21:10.01,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,No, time spent remembering \Nsomeone lost is time well spent.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.42,0:21:14.31,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,Now, let me introduce you \Nto your new team.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.31,0:21:16.63,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,Right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.63,0:21:17.64,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.64,0:21:19.61,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,Hey, is that really her?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.61,0:21:21.09,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,I'm sure a lot's happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.64,0:21:22.99,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,You got that right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.96,0:21:37.39,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I am Colonel Vladilena Milizé \Nof the San Magnolia Republic.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.72,0:21:39.07,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,It's an honor to meet you \Nfor the first time.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.50,0:21:43.45,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,This isn't the first time we've met.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.79,0:21:47.43,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,It's the first time \Nwe've seen each other, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.36,0:21:53.08,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,It's been a long time, \NHandler One.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.76,0:21:58.55,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I am a Captain in the Giad Federacy,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.24,0:22:01.75,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,and the former combat commander \Nof Spearhead Squadron,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.28,0:22:03.97,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Shinei Nouzen.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.59,0:22:17.73,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Shin...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.09,0:22:45.31,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Kitty!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.09,0:22:45.31,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Machiavelli!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.09,0:22:45.31,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Blackie!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.09,0:22:45.31,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Whitey!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.39,0:22:50.08,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,You really are a fool, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.90,0:22:52.24,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Raiden!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.24,0:22:53.71,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Is this us?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.92,0:22:55.14,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Theo!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.14,0:22:58.18,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Thank you for the cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.18,0:22:59.29,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Anju!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.29,0:23:01.08,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,I'm glad you're alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.08,0:23:02.19,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Kurena!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.19,0:23:05.06,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,How about we take a photo \Nto remember today?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.30,0:23:07.23,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,That's a great idea!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.12,0:23:13.86,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I followed you for so long.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.33,0:23:15.59,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.93,0:23:17.45,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I've finally caught up.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.98,0:23:18.78,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,You have.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.07,0:23:22.36,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,From now on...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.73,0:23:25.95,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I'll fight with you.
